			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Add robust state recovery primitives with backoff and timeout\n\nExtract core recovery logic into dedicated PascalCase modules under `RecoverState` to enforce the project's `Struct::Struct` naming convention and isolate failure handling for `ApplicationState`.\n\nIntroduce three new utilities:\n1. `RecoverStateWithBackoff`: Implements exponential backoff (100ms doubling) for async recovery operations, yielding the runtime during wait periods.\n2. `SafeStateOperationWithTimeout`: Executes blocking state operations on a detached thread with a hard timeout to prevent hung repairs from stalling the main event loop.\n3. `ValidateAndCleanState`: Filters state maps in-place using a validator predicate, logging removals for observability.\n\nThese components provide the atomic building blocks required for the `MementoLoader` to handle corrupted `ApplicationState` gracefully, ensuring the editor can degrade to a clean state without crashing during startup or recovery flows.",
			"SHA": "9b58d4d4e5ff9f5e01e82549344e29bbc6c4b021"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
