			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Eliminate IPC re-exports and migrate to legacy server\n\nRemove all `pub use` re-exports from `Source/IPC/mod.rs` to enforce explicit `Struct::Struct` import paths, aligning with the project's strict naming convention and recent entry-point refactoring. Callers must now reference the full nested path (e.g., `IPC::Connection::Manager::ConnectionManager`).\n\nSimultaneously, redirect IPC server instance references in `ConfigurationBridge.rs` and `StatusReporter.rs` from `TauriIPCServer` to `TauriIPCServer_Old`. This ensures compatibility with the current legacy server instance while the new implementation stabilizes. Add documentation to `AdvancedFeatures` noting the plan to atomize the 648-LOC single file into a directory.\n\nThis change reduces module resolution ambiguity and maintains IPC continuity during the ongoing architecture migration.",
			"SHA": "c85b6b3f4fceb80e8171ca8abe9de66da6baf67b"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-02T06:37:17Z",
